# Clinical Trial EDC Data Validation & Edit Check Specifications

**Protocol No.:** CTJ301UC201 
**Document Date:** 16 May 2017 (Ver. 1.1) 
**Sponsor:** Leading Biopharm Limited 
**Domain Coverage:** Demographics (DM), Routine Haematology (RH), Routine Clinical Chemistry (RCC) 

---

## 📌 Project Overview
This document specifies the Data Clarification Form (DCF) logic, boundary conditions, and cross-form validation rules for an Electronic Data Capture (EDC) system. Designed for screening visit data collection, these edit checks automatically flag out-of-range values, invalid data types, and missing fields to ensure data integrity during Clinical Data Management (CDM).

---

## 🛠️ Validation Specifications

### 1. Demography [DM]

| Variable | Field Name | Format / Constraints | Logic & Query Triggers |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `DM_GD` | Gender | Checkbox (0 = Male, 1 = Female) | Raise query if no option is selected. |
| `DM_DOB` | Date of Birth | `DD/MM/YY` (6 digits) | Allow numerical values only. Raise query if alphabet/decimal entry made or left blank. |
| `DM_RC` | Race | Checkbox (0 = Caucasian, 1 = Black, 2 = Oriental, 3 = Others) | Raise query if no option is selected. |
| `DM_EO` | Ethnic Origin | Checkbox (0 = Asian, 1 = Black, 2 = White, 3 = Indigenous, 4 = Hispanic, 5 = Latino) | Optional field. Entry can be left blank if ethnic origin cannot be disclosed. |

---

### 2. Routine Haematology [RH]
*General Constraint: Numerical values only, limited to 3 digits unless specified. Decimals allowed. Raise query if alphabetic input is entered or length constraints are violated.*

| Variable | Parameter | Reference Range | Specific Edit Checks & Query Logic |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `RH_HCT` | Hematocrit | Male: 41–50% <br> Female: 36–44% | Cross-checks `DM_GD`: <br>• Raise query if Male and value = 40 <br>• Raise query if Female and value = 35 |
| `RH_HB` | Haemoglobin | Male: 13.5–16 g/dL <br> Female: 12.5–14.5 g/dL | Cross-checks `DM_GD`: <br>• Raise query if general value $\le 13.5$ or $\ge 16$ <br>• Raise query if Male and value = 13.4 <br>• Raise query if Female and value = 12.4 |
| `RH_MCH` | Mean Cellular Haemoglobin | 27–32 pg | Raise query if value = 26 |
| `RH_MCHC` | Mean Cellular Haemoglobin Conc. | 31.5–34.5 g/dL | Raise query if value = 31 |
| `RH_MCV` | Mean Cellular Volume | 83–101 fL | Raise query if value = 82 |
| `RH_PTC` | Platelet Count | 1.50–4.50 lakhs cells/mm³ | Raise query if value = 1.40 |
| `RH_RBC` | Red Blood Cell Count | 4–5 million cells/µL | Raise query if value = 3 |
| `RH_WBC` | White Blood Cell Count | 4,000–10,000 cells/mm³ | Limit: 4 to 5 digits (no less than 4). Raise query if value = 3,999 |
| `RH_NPL` | Neutrophils | 40–70% | Raise query if value = 39 |
| `RH_LMP` | Lymphocytes | 20–40% | Raise query if value = 19 |
| `RH_MNC` | Monocytes | 2–10% | Max 2 digits. Raise query if value = 11 |
| `RH_ESP` | Eosinophils | 0–6% | Max 2 digits. Raise query if value = 7 |
| `RH_BSL` | Basophils | 0–1% | Max 2 digits (e.g., 0.5). Raise query if value = 2 |

